WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.550
In March 2025, a dozen eggs in the US

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.520
cost a record 6.23 dollars on average.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.330
Bird flu had forced producers
to cull millions of hens.

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.240
Shoppers and bakeries bought fewer eggs.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.330
Importers shipped in
millions of eggs from abroad.

6
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.300
Nobody ordered any of it.

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.230
So with no one in charge,

8
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.790
how do millions of
buyers and sellers end up

9
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.870
producing what people want?

10
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll
see how one market shock

11
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.110
sets off three different responses.

12
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.220
Then you'll shift demand yourself
and watch a shortage close.

13
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: explain how a market
coordinates millions of choices.
